  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Find the gradients of the three lines $5x-7y+5=0$, $2x-5y+7=0$ and $7x+5y+2=0$. Show that they enclose a right-angled triangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m_1=\\frac57$, $m_2=\\frac25$, $m_3=-\\frac75$. Since $m_1m_3=-1$, lines 1 and 3 are perpendicular, so the triangle is right-angled.",
      "worked": "Line 1:\n$$\\begin{aligned}7y&=5x+5\\\\y&=\\frac57x+\\frac57\\\\m_1&=\\frac57\\end{aligned}$$\nLine 2:\n$$\\begin{aligned}5y&=2x+7\\\\y&=\\frac25x+\\frac75\\\\m_2&=\\frac25\\end{aligned}$$\nLine 3:\n$$\\begin{aligned}5y&=-7x-2\\\\y&=-\\frac75x-\\frac25\\\\m_3&=-\\frac75\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}m_1m_3&=\\frac57\\times\\left(-\\frac75\\right)\\\\&=-1\\end{aligned}$$\nLines 1 and 3 are perpendicular, so the triangle is right-angled.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
